## Claim
Text: "US Democratic presidential nominee Joe Biden was endorsed by Black Lives Matter and Antifa"
Claim date: October 10, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### As of October 10, 2020, was Joe Biden the official presidential nominee of the US Democratic Party?
Answer: Yes, as of October 10, 2020, Joe Biden was the official presidential nominee of the US Democratic Party, having formally accepted the nomination at the Democratic National Convention in August 2020. The source states, "Joe Biden is formally accepting the Democratic Party’s nomination for president on Thursday at the Democratic National Convention."

Source URL: https://witf.org/2020/08/20/fact-check-joe-bidens-speech-at-the-democratic-national-convention/

### Is there a single, centralized organization with the official name "Black Lives Matter" that makes political endorsements for candidates?
Answer: The search result, an opinion piece, refers to "the organization Black Lives Matter" and describes financial links between BLM's website and the Democratic fundraising platform ActBlue, but it does not provide specific information about whether a single, centralized Black Lives Matter organization has an official process for making political endorsements for candidates. The article's focus is on fundraising flows and political alignment, not on endorsement procedures.

Source URL: https://wbsm.com/democrats-are-endorsing-mob-mentality-across-america-opinion/

### Did any official chapter, affiliated group, or recognized leadership body of the Black Lives Matter movement issue a public statement endorsing Joe Biden for president prior to or on October 10, 2020?
Answer: No official chapter, affiliated group, or recognized leadership body of Black Lives Matter endorsed Joe Biden; in fact, a co-founder publicly opposed his candidacy. In February 2020, Patrisse Cullors explicitly stated, "It’s important that we beat the Bloombergs of the world and the Bidens of the world," and endorsed Bernie Sanders and Elizabeth Warren instead.

Source URL: https://www.newsweek.com/black-lives-matter-co-founder-endorses-sanders-warren-1488912

### What was the specific wording of any statement from a Black Lives Matter-affiliated group that is cited as an endorsement of Joe Biden?
Answer: The search result does not contain any specific statement or wording from a Black Lives Matter-affiliated group endorsing Joe Biden; it only describes a Biden campaign ad that features imagery of Black Lives Matter posters.

Source URL: https://apnews.com/article/virus-outbreak-election-2020-ap-top-news-race-and-ethnicity-entertainment-95669df17e248bbfeb1ba5975a087cf1

### Is there a single, centralized organization with the official name "Antifa" that makes political endorsements for candidates?
Answer: No, according to the search result, there is no single, centralized organization called "Antifa"; FBI Director Christopher Wray testified that antifa is "not a group or an organization. It’s a movement or an ideology."

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/01/fact-check-quote-attributed-biden-antifa-missing-context/5885435002/

### Did Joe Biden's presidential campaign publicly acknowledge or accept an endorsement from either "Black Lives Matter" or "Antifa" around this time?
Answer: No, Joe Biden's campaign did not publicly acknowledge or accept an endorsement from either Black Lives Matter or Antifa. The search result directly quotes Alicia Garza, a co-founder of the Black Lives Matter movement, stating that the Biden campaign was "pretty far from the concerns that this movement has put forward" and urging activists to "push him to be a better candidate." There is no mention in the source of any formal endorsement being given or accepted.

Source URL: https://time.com/5867282/alicia-garza-black-lives-matter-biden/

### Have representatives of the Black Lives Matter movement or of groups associated with Antifa publicly denied or clarified the claim that they endorsed Joe Biden?
Answer: Yes, a Black Lives Matter co-founder explicitly opposed Joe Biden's candidacy rather than endorsing him. Patrisse Cullors stated she was endorsing Bernie Sanders and Elizabeth Warren, saying, "It's important that we beat the Bloombergs of the world and the Bidens of the world," and added that for Biden, "it should be time for him to stand down." The search result does not contain information regarding groups associated with Antifa.

Source URL: https://www.newsweek.com/black-lives-matter-co-founder-endorses-sanders-warren-1488912

## Final Judgement
The key findings from the fact-check are that while Joe Biden was indeed the official Democratic nominee by October 10, 2020, there is no evidence supporting the claim that he received an endorsement from either Black Lives Matter (BLM) or Antifa. Regarding BLM, the evidence shows that a co-founder publicly opposed his candidacy in early 2020, and there is no record of any official chapter, group, or recognized leadership body issuing a public endorsement. For Antifa, the evidence establishes it is not a centralized organization capable of issuing formal endorsements. Furthermore, Biden's campaign did not acknowledge or accept any such endorsement.

No information was found indicating any official endorsement was issued by a recognized body of Black Lives Matter or any structured Antifa organization. The evidence explicitly contradicts the notion of a formal BLM endorsement.

The recorded evidence clearly refutes the claim that Joe Biden was endorsed by Black Lives Matter and Antifa. Therefore, the decision is `refuted`.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim is refuted by the evidence gathered. While Joe Biden was the official Democratic nominee as of October 10, 2020, the record shows no evidence of an endorsement from either group. A co-founder of the Black Lives Matter movement, Patrisse Cullors, publicly opposed Biden's candidacy and endorsed other candidates, stating it was important to "beat the Bloombergs of the world and the Bidens of the world" ([Newsweek](https://www.newsweek.com/black-lives-matter-co-founder-endorses-sanders-warren-1488912)). Additionally, there is no record of any official BLM chapter or leadership body issuing a formal endorsement. Regarding Antifa, FBI Director Christopher Wray testified that it is "not a group or an organization" but rather "a movement or an ideology," meaning it lacks the centralized structure to issue political endorsements ([USA Today](https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/10/01/fact-check-quote-attributed-biden-antifa-missing-context/5885435002/)). Furthermore, Biden's campaign did not publicly acknowledge or accept any such endorsements ([Time](https://time.com/5867282/alicia-garza-black-lives-matter-biden/)).